                <pb facs="0137" n="49" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg49"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No.
                    220.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The judge will decree a provisional setting aside of the case when there shall
                    appear only prima facie proof of the offense, or this being fully proved there
                    result only slight presumptions against the accused; and then he will set it
                    aside definitively.</p>
                <p>1. When from the summary statement it results that the offense has not existed
                    for which the accused is prosecuted, or the fact which is investigated is not
                    legally punishable.</p>
                <p>(Article 186, code of criminal instruction of Nicaragua.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
